===================================================
    
Case 1: 64-partition inner, 12,000 outer rows -> hash join     

===================================================
count(*)    
120000     

Query plan:
hash-join (inner join)
    edge:  term[?]
    outer: sscan
               class: o node[?]
               sargs: term[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    inner: sscan
               class: w node[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select /*+ PARALLEL(?) */ count(*) from t_o o, t_p? w where w.k=o.k and ( mod(o.k, ?)=? or ((o.k= ?:? ) or (o.k> ?:? )))
===================================================
    
Case 2: the partition key is the join key, it does not prune per row -> hash join     

===================================================
count(*)    
120000     

Query plan:
hash-join (inner join)
    edge:  term[?]
    outer: sscan
               class: o node[?]
               sargs: term[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    inner: sscan
               class: w node[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select /*+ PARALLEL(?) */ count(*) from t_o o, t_pk? w where w.k=o.k and ( mod(o.k, ?)=? or ((o.k= ?:? ) or (o.k> ?:? )))
===================================================
    
Case 3: the same join on a table that is not partitioned keeps the index nested loop     

===================================================
count(*)    
120000     

Query plan:
idx-join (inner join)
    outer: sscan
               class: o node[?]
               sargs: term[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    inner: iscan
               class: w node[?]
               index: i_np term[?] (covers)
               cost:  ? card ?
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select /*+ PARALLEL(?) */ count(*) from t_o o, t_np w where w.k=o.k and ( mod(o.k, ?)=? or ((o.k= ?:? ) or (o.k> ?:? )))
===================================================
    
Case 4: a few outer rows keep the index nested loop on the 64-partition inner     

===================================================
count(*)    
90     

Query plan:
idx-join (inner join)
    outer: iscan
               class: o node[?]
               index: pk_t_o_id term[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    inner: iscan
               class: w node[?]
               index: i_p? term[?] (covers)
               cost:  ? card ?
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select /*+ PARALLEL(?) */ count(*) from t_o o, t_p? w where w.k=o.k and (o.id< ?:? )
===================================================
    
Case 5: NOT EXISTS followed by a join to the 64-partition table -> hash join     

===================================================
count(*)    
100000     

Query plan:
hash-join (inner join)
    edge:  term[?]
    outer: hash-join (anti join)
               edge:  term[?]
               outer: sscan
                          class: o node[?]
                          cost:  ? card ?
               inner: sscan
                          class: x node[?]
                          cost:  ? card ?
               cost:  ? card ?
    inner: sscan
               class: w node[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select /*+ PARALLEL(?) */ count(*) from t_o o anti join t_half x on x.k=o.k, t_p? w where w.k=o.k
===================================================
    
Case 6: EXISTS followed by a join to the 64-partition table -> hash join     

===================================================
count(*)    
100000     

Query plan:
hash-join (inner join)
    edge:  term[?]
    outer: hash-join (inner join)
               edge:  term[?]
               outer: temp(distinct)
                          subplan: sscan
                                       class: x node[?]
                                       cost:  ? card ?
                          cost:  ? card ?
               inner: sscan
                          class: o node[?]
                          cost:  ? card ?
               cost:  ? card ?
    inner: sscan
               class: w node[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select /*+ PARALLEL(?) */ count(*) from t_o o semi join t_half x on x.k=o.k, t_p? w where w.k=o.k
===================================================
    
